---
import ServiceLayout from '../../components/templates/ServiceLayout.astro';
import { serviceBySlug, towns } from '../../lib/business';

const service = serviceBySlug('web-design')!;
const townLinks = towns.map((t) => ({
  href: `/web-design-${t.slug}`,
  label: `${t.name}, OR`,
  sub: t.county,
}));
---

<ServiceLayout
  service={service}
  title="Web Design for Oregon Coast Businesses · Winters Code"
  description="Custom web design for Coos and Curry County businesses. Mobile-first, fast, and built for your customer. Not a template, not WordPress. Live in days."
  eyebrow="Services · Web Design"
  h1="Web design built for your customer."
  sub="Custom design for Oregon coast businesses. Mobile-first, fast, and shaped around the one thing your customer came to do."
  sub2="Not a template. Not a builder. Yours."
  bgImage="/photo/local/facerock-sunset"
  showcase
  heroFocal="center 38%"
  intro={[
    "Good web design is not decoration. It is the shortest path between a stranger on their phone and the thing they need from you: a booking, a quote, a phone call. I design every page around that path first, then make it look like it <span class='hl-green'>belongs to your business</span>.",
    "Every build starts with one question. <em>What story does this site need to tell?</em> For a charter captain that might be: here is the boat, here is the dock, book a trip. For a lodge it is a full visual narrative. I figure out which one fits, then design to it.",
  ]}
  includes={[
    { h: 'Mobile-first layout', body: 'Designed for the phone first, because that is where your customers actually are. It scales up to desktop, never the other way around.' },
    { h: 'Custom design', body: 'Drawn for your business, not pulled from a theme. Your colors, your photos, your voice. Nothing looks stamped from a template.' },
    { h: 'Built to convert', body: 'Clear calls to action, a phone number one tap away, and a path to the booking or the brief that does not make people think.' },
    { h: 'SEO foundations', body: 'Clean headings, real metadata, fast loads, and structured data baked in from the start so search engines understand the site.' },
    { h: 'Accessible by default', body: 'Keyboard navigation, real contrast, and semantic markup. It reads well for everyone and ranks better for it.' },
    { h: 'Yours to keep', body: 'You own the code and the content. No platform lock-in, no monthly rent to keep your own site online.' },
  ]}
  whyTitle="Why custom, and the proof"
  why={[
    "Every web shop says the same line now: <em>we write code, not templates.</em> Fair enough. It is also what the out-of-area agencies say on the identical page they publish for four hundred other towns. So do not take the claim. Take the numbers.",
    "I audited <span class='stat'>169</span> Coos County small-business websites with Google Lighthouse and Mozilla Observatory. Average mobile speed: <span class='stat'>61/100</span>. Not one scored both fast and secure. The three platforms most businesses rent from, WordPress, Squarespace, and Wix, averaged a <span class='hl-copper'>D, an F, and a C</span>. Custom code, the kind I build, averaged <span class='stat'>94</span> on mobile with an <span class='hl-copper'>A-plus</span> security grade.",
    "That gap is the whole opportunity. Most local sites are rented, not owned: slow, plugin-heavy, and breaking at 2 AM when something auto-updates. A fast, custom site does not just look better. It <span class='hl-green'>outranks the rented sites around it, and the phone rings.</span>",
    "And when something needs changing, you text the person who built it. <em>Not a ticket queue. Not a call center. Me.</em>",
  ]}
  faq={[
    { q: 'How long does a website take?', a: 'A typical small business site is live in about 3 to 7 business days. Larger sites with custom features run 1 to 2 weeks, and bigger custom builds 2 to 4 weeks. I work in days, not quarters.' },
    { q: 'How does the build actually go?', a: 'Short version: questionnaire, then a consult, then a signed scope and deposit, then I build, then it goes live. The full step-by-step is on the <a href="/process">process page</a>.' },
    { q: 'Do you design on WordPress or a builder?', a: 'No. It is custom code. WordPress and builders are mass-produced software with plugins stacked on top: slower, plugin-dependent, and prone to breaking at 2 AM when something auto-updates. Custom code loads faster, ranks better, and stays secure.' },
    { q: 'What if I do not have photos or copy yet?', a: 'I do most of the lift. A short questionnaire gets us started, and I can shoot real photos of your business and draft the copy for you to edit. No stock photography unless you want it.' },
    { q: 'Will my site work on phones?', a: 'It is designed for phones first. On the Oregon coast most local searches happen on a phone over rural LTE, so sub-second mobile loads are the whole point, not an afterthought.' },
  ]}
  relatedTitle="Web design across Coos and Curry counties"
  relatedIntro="Local pages for the towns I serve. Same fast, custom build, tuned to each town."
  relatedLinks={townLinks}
/>
